WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:11.290
TriedPath Fellowship presents:

2
00:00:11.290 --> 00:00:13.157
Understanding Your Roots.

3
00:00:14.107 --> 00:00:16.194
Part one. How your mind works.

4
00:00:16.294 --> 00:00:18.495
Our mind works like a computer.

5
00:00:18.495 --> 00:00:22.259
It is constantly placing information into
categories.

6
00:00:22.359 --> 00:00:25.557
If you feed something destructive into
your mind,

7
00:00:25.557 --> 00:00:29.603
it will add this to a stack of similar
material already there.

8
00:00:29.703 --> 00:00:32.452
As the stack grows larger, it gains in
power.

9
00:00:32.552 --> 00:00:35.425
In the computer industry, the saying is:

10
00:00:35.425 --> 00:00:37.148
garbage in, garbage out.

11
00:00:37.848 --> 00:00:41.577
It is our responsibility to see that the
new information

12
00:00:41.577 --> 00:00:44.440
we receive is consistent with our new
life.

13
00:00:45.590 --> 00:00:48.333
New from TriedPath: Mountains of Material!

14
00:00:48.283 --> 00:00:51.070
Scripture memory, on twelve cassettes.

15
00:00:51.070 --> 00:00:54.297
In the car. In the kitchen. At your
bedside.

16
00:00:54.247 --> 00:00:55.670
Fill your memory tapes,

17
00:00:55.670 --> 00:00:57.526
and push the old material out!

18
00:00:57.426 --> 00:00:59.145
Operators are standing by!

19
00:01:00.895 --> 00:01:03.002
End of part one. Question two.

20
00:01:03.002 --> 00:01:07.004
Have you ever been able to stop thinking
about something?

21
00:01:07.004 --> 00:01:08.128
Did you succeed?

22
00:01:08.128 --> 00:01:10.796
Pause the tape, and write your answer.

23
00:01:16.346 --> 00:01:18.185
Part two. Your roots.

24
00:01:18.285 --> 00:01:20.171
You were not born this way.

25
00:01:20.171 --> 00:01:22.405
It grew, one response at a time.

26
00:01:22.405 --> 00:01:25.059
And what was learned can be unlearned.

27
00:01:26.459 --> 00:01:29.316
A child's security rests on three bonds:

28
00:01:29.316 --> 00:01:31.673
mother to child, father to child,

29
00:01:31.673 --> 00:01:33.173
and father to mother.

30
00:01:33.273 --> 00:01:36.660
Any break in this triangle produces
insecurity.

31
00:01:36.660 --> 00:01:38.389
Real, or only perceived,

32
00:01:38.389 --> 00:01:40.191
the results are the same.

33
00:01:42.891 --> 00:01:46.422
Between two and six, a boy must leave his
mother's world,

34
00:01:46.422 --> 00:01:49.210
and his father must welcome him into his
own.

35
00:01:51.310 --> 00:01:53.872
But a boy with no welcome from his father

36
00:01:53.872 --> 00:01:55.497
finds none among the boys.

37
00:01:55.497 --> 00:01:58.246
So he stays in the kitchen, with his
mother.

38
00:01:59.946 --> 00:02:02.728
He compares himself with other boys.

39
00:02:02.728 --> 00:02:05.047
Comparison becomes admiration.

40
00:02:05.047 --> 00:02:07.134
Admiration slips into envy.

41
00:02:07.234 --> 00:02:10.037
At puberty, the envy becomes eroticized.

42
00:02:11.237 --> 00:02:12.950
Part three. Displacement.

43
00:02:12.950 --> 00:02:14.594
Putting off, putting on.

44
00:02:14.694 --> 00:02:18.762
Displacement is the idea that one thing
pushes out another.

45
00:02:18.762 --> 00:02:20.624
There is no neutral ground.

46
00:02:20.724 --> 00:02:23.551
If there is a vacancy there, evil will
fill it.

47
00:02:23.651 --> 00:02:27.100
Interference is the technical name for
displacement.

48
00:02:27.100 --> 00:02:31.278
New material coming into your mind pushes
the old material out.

49
00:02:31.378 --> 00:02:34.100
In thirty days, we forget eighty percent

50
00:02:34.100 --> 00:02:35.393
of what we learned.

51
00:02:35.393 --> 00:02:37.298
For you, that is a blessing.

52
00:02:38.698 --> 00:02:42.196
Turn on any radio or television, and you
will find

53
00:02:42.196 --> 00:02:45.764
a mind-boggling barrage of new morality
propaganda.

54
00:02:45.864 --> 00:02:49.067
Gays on television are shown as superior
people.

55
00:02:52.067 --> 00:02:53.330
What do we lose?

56
00:02:53.330 --> 00:02:57.041
The associations, triggered by music,
clothing,

57
00:02:57.041 --> 00:02:58.778
and many other things.

58
00:02:58.778 --> 00:03:01.857
Bars will close. The scene will change.

59
00:03:02.257 --> 00:03:03.251
Question five.

60
00:03:03.251 --> 00:03:07.585
What do you do when associations from the
past overwhelm you?

61
00:03:07.585 --> 00:03:10.284
Pause the tape, and write your answer.

62
00:03:12.784 --> 00:03:15.699
So fill your memory tapes with new
material,

63
00:03:15.699 --> 00:03:18.084
until the bulk of it ejects the old.

64
00:03:18.784 --> 00:03:21.880
We forget things that are contrary to our
opinions.

65
00:03:21.980 --> 00:03:24.855
If we are ambivalent, the new information

66
00:03:24.855 --> 00:03:27.730
will find no permanent home in our minds.

67
00:03:27.730 --> 00:03:30.395
This places the burden directly on us.

68
00:03:31.795 --> 00:03:33.080
For further study:

69
00:03:33.080 --> 00:03:35.722
booklet one, from our Pocket Library.

70
00:03:36.172 --> 00:03:38.978
Homosexual people say they never asked

71
00:03:38.978 --> 00:03:40.602
for their orientation.

72
00:03:40.602 --> 00:03:42.670
In most cases, that is true.

73
00:03:42.970 --> 00:03:44.692
Something they never chose.
